wat Valley in Pakistan. Malala courageously defied the rules and kept going to school."}, {"time": "28000", "image": "engenn6le02ob09re2img02.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "Her life was under threat and at times she had to go into hiding. Finally, at the age of 15 Malala was tragically shot and almost killed by the Taliban on her way home from school. But Malala miraculously survived. The Taliban thought they could silence her but instead have given her an even stronger voice, which can now be heard all over the world."}, {"time": "52000", "image": "engenn6le02ob09re2img03.jpg", "id": 3, "text": "Malala has continued on her fight to advocate for every child's right to an education. She strongly believes that education is the future, and that one child, one teacher, one book and one pen can change the world."}]}}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "audio", "id": 1, "_data": []}, {"contents": [{"type": "audio", "value": "engenn6le02ob09re6aud01"}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "text", "id": 2, "_data": []}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}], "type": "lab_options"}]}], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Famous People"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Malala Yousafzai"}, {"type": "position", "content": 9}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Accurately use information about people in communicative situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn6le02ob09re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Simple Past vs Present Perfect"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect</span> tense to talk about a finished action or event that is connected to the present in some way.</p>   You use the <span class=\"strong\">Simple Past</span> tense to talk about a finished action or event <span class=\"strong\">not</span> necessarily connected to the present."}, {"type": "example", "content": "She has received a prize."}, {"type": "example", "content": "She spoke up for the rights of others."}, {"type": "example", "content": "She has changed the world."}, {"type": "text", "content": "We use <span class=\"strong\">have/has</span> + <span class=\"strong\">the past participle</span> of the verb in Present Perfect sentences."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Adverbs of Manner"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">adverbs of manner</span> to describe how something is done.</p>  Example: She strongly believes that each child deserves the right to an education.</p>  How does she believe? Strongly."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Many adverbs are formed by adding -ly to an adjective.</p>  You take out the letter -y and add -ily to adjectives ending in -y.</p>  Some adjectives do not change when they become adverbs."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adjective\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adverb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"courageous</br> strong</br>\\t\\t tragic</br>\\t\\t miraculous</br> happy</br>\\t well\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"courageously</br> strongly</br> tragically</br> miraculously</br> happily</br> well\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to speak out"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to say something when you do not have the power to say it "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Malala spoke out for girls' rights at the age of 11. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le02ob09aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about people you admire."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "courageous"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "brave"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Malala is a courageous girl.  "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le02ob09aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to defy"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to refuse to do what someone in power tells you to do "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Malala defied the rules set by the Taliban. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le02ob09aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "miraculous"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "very good; completely unexpected; very lucky"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  She had a miraculous recovery. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le02ob09aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to advocate"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to publicly say that something should be done"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Malala advocates for a child's rights to education."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le02ob09aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Go to this wesbsite: <br/> http://webtv.un.org/watch/malala-yousafzai-addresses-united-nations-youth-assembly/2542094251001/"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Watch Malala's speech. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "After you have finished watching the video, answer these questions:<br/> a. How did you feel while you watched the speech?  <br/> b. What is the main message in Malala's speech to the United Nations?  <br/> c. What is she asking the world leaders to do? <br/> d. What do you think of Malala?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write down your answers. Share them with a partner. Listen to their answers."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I listen to a speech."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I describe how I feel about a person."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about a person's past experiences."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I share my opinion about Malala."}]}]}